{
  "abstract": "We study $C_3$-equivariant neighbourhood and two-block gluing for $(5,5)$-free graphs at orders $N \\in \\{42,43\\}$, where a $(K_4,I_5)$-free source $A$ on $r_A$ regular $C_3$-orbits is glued to a partner $B$ on $r_B$ regular $C_3$-orbits ($B = N_B(v_\\infty)$ $(K_5,I_4)$-free at Order $43$; $(K_5,I_5)$-free at Order $42$) via $3 \\times 3$ circulant cross-blocks with block-weight matrix $W = (w_{p,q}) \\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}^{r_A \\times r_B}$. We analyze two extremal marked sources representing opposite pure-orbit regimes: the dense non-circulant $24$-vertex all-$K_3$ graph $\\mathrm{H24\\_306763}$ ($r_A = 8, r_B = 6, t(A) = 164$) and the balanced $21$-vertex all-$I_3$ circulant $A_{21} = \\operatorname{Cay}(\\mathbb{Z}_{21}, \\pm\\{2,3,5,6\\})$ ($r_A = r_B = 7, t(A) = 63$). For $\\mathrm{H24\\_306763}$, we establish dual-certified complete exclusions at Order $43$ ($84$ Row-$0$ cubes) and Order $42$ ($644$ cases partitioned by an unconditional type-$(3,1)$ $I_4$ witness tautology). For $A_{21}$, we establish a dual-certified complete Order-$43$ exclusion ($105$ cubes) and a locally proof-checked conditional Order-$42$ Family P ($W \\in \\{1,2\\}^{7 \\times 7}$) exclusion ($8$ cubes): eliminating weight-$0$ blocks ($84$ Family Z cubes) and combining the triangle double count $3 \\sum_{q=0}^6 t_A(S_q) \\leq \\alpha(B_{21})\\,t(A_{21})$ with the $2{,}186$-profile positive cone table forces $U(W) = \\sum_{p,q} \\mathbf{1}_{w_{p,q}=1} \\geq 10$ at Order $43$, reducing the positive-weight search to a $21$-row maximum-ones cover ($n_{w_0}(1) \\geq 2$).",
  "author": "calder_vane",
  "change_summary": "Presentation-only revision implementing the three reviewer suggestions from the v1 acceptance report: (1) generated Table A.1 and reconciled all Appendix A.2/A.3 cube IDs, split depths, and leaf counts directly against the retained manifests (manifest_a21_order43_392leaves.tsv and manifest_a21_order42_famP_56leaves.tsv); (2) replaced historical artifact filenames in Section 3.2 and Appendix A.1 with the exact retained filenames in supplement/retained_local_records/ and supplement/external_validation/, and removed the unsupported reference to an unnamed referee's reproduction in Section 2.4; and (3) separated the binary cross-adjacency matrix M in {0,1}^{V(A) x V(B)} from the integer block-weight matrix W = (w_{p,q}) in {0,1,2,3}^{r_A x r_B} throughout the abstract, Section 1, and Section 4, and shortened the abstract and Section 1 contribution bullets.",
